## ✅ Flow Complete — `VendorInvoiceProcessing.flow`

### What it does

| Step | Node | What happens |
|---|---|---|
| **Trigger** | New File in SharePoint | Fires automatically whenever a PDF lands in your **New Vendor** folder — polling mode, PDF-only filter |
| **Download** | Download Invoice PDF | Fetches the PDF from SharePoint using the file's reference ID |
| **Extract** | Extract Invoice Fields | Runs the **InvoiceIXP** model — pulls Invoice Number, Invoice Date, Due Date, PO Number, Currency, Vendor Name, Total Amount, Total Due, Payment Terms, Subtotal, Tax Amount |
| **Parse** | Parse Invoice Fields | Script node maps the extracted field array into clean named properties |
| **Post to SAP** | Post Invoice to SAP | HTTP POST to your SAP endpoint with all the invoice fields as JSON |
| **Success terminal** | Done — Invoice Posted | Flow ends cleanly on success |
| **Error handling** | Log Download Error / Log Extract Error / Log SAP Error | Each step has its own error branch that logs the failure details |
| **Error terminal** | Done — Error | All error paths converge here |

### One thing to do before it can run

The SAP URL is currently a placeholder — `https://YOUR-SAP-ENDPOINT/api/invoices`. Ask your IT team for the actual endpoint address, then open the **Post Invoice to SAP** node in Studio Web and replace it.

